@startuml Raft Consensus Protocol for Stock Allocation

' Professional Color Palette
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 2
skinparam roundcorner 10
skinparam ParticipantFontSize 11
skinparam ParticipantFontStyle bold

!define LEADER_COLOR #B71C1C
!define FOLLOWER_COLOR #6A1B9A
!define CLIENT_COLOR #1976D2
!define LOG_COLOR #F57C00

title <size:18><color:#B71C1C><b>Raft Consensus Protocol</b></color></size> <size:12><color:#424242>Distributed Stock Allocation with Linearizability</color></size>

' ============================================
' Participants
' ============================================

participant "<color:white><b>Client</b> (Inventory Service)</color>" as Client CLIENT_COLOR
participant "<color:white><b>Raft Leader</b> (Node 1)</color>" as Leader LEADER_COLOR
participant "<color:white><b>Raft Follower</b> (Node 2)</color>" as Follower1 FOLLOWER_COLOR
participant "<color:white><b>Raft Follower</b> (Node 3)</color>" as Follower2 FOLLOWER_COLOR
database "<color:white><b>Log</b> (Leader)</color>" as LogLeader LOG_COLOR
database "<color:white><b>Log</b> (Follower 1)</color>" as LogF1 LOG_COLOR
database "<color:white><b>Log</b> (Follower 2)</color>" as LogF2 LOG_COLOR

' ============================================
' Scenario 1: Normal Operation
' ============================================

== Scenario 1: Normal Operation - Stock Reservation ==

Client -> Leader : <b>AppendEntry Request</b> SKU: IPHONE-15, qty: 1 contractId: ctr_123
activate Leader #FFCDD2

note right of Client #E3F2FD
  <b><color:#1976D2>Request</color></b>
  ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
  <b>Operation:</b> RESERVE_STOCK
  <b>SKU:</b> IPHONE-15
  <b>Quantity:</b> 1
  <b>Warehouse:</b> NY
  <b>Contract:</b> ctr_123
end note

Leader -> LogLeader : <b>Append to log</b> Index: 100 Term: 5
activate LogLeader #FFE0B2
LogLeader --> Leader : OK
deactivate LogLeader

note right of Leader #FFEBEE
  <b><color:#B71C1C>Leader Responsibilities</color></b>
  ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
  1. Append to local log
  2. Replicate to followers
  3. Wait for quorum (majority)
  4. Commit when majority confirmed
  5. Notify followers to commit
end note

par <color:#6A1B9A><b>Replicate to Followers in Parallel</b></color>

    Leader -> Follower1 : <b>AppendEntries RPC</b> Index: 100, Term: 5 Operation: RESERVE_STOCK
    activate Follower1 #E1BEE7

    Follower1 -> LogF1 : Append to log
    activate LogF1 #FFE0B2
    LogF1 --> Follower1 : OK
    deactivate LogF1

    Follower1 --> Leader : ✅ <b>ACK</b> (Index: 100)
    deactivate Follower1

else <color:#6A1B9A><b>Parallel Path</b></color>

    Leader -> Follower2 : <b>AppendEntries RPC</b> Index: 100, Term: 5 Operation: RESERVE_STOCK
    activate Follower2 #E1BEE7

    Follower2 -> LogF2 : Append to log
    activate LogF2 #FFE0B2
    LogF2 --> Follower2 : OK
    deactivate LogF2

    Follower2 --> Leader : ✅ <b>ACK</b> (Index: 100)
    deactivate Follower2

end

Leader -> Leader : <b>Quorum achieved</b> (2 out of 3 nodes) → Commit entry

note right of Leader #FFEBEE
  <b><color:#B71C1C>Quorum Calculation</color></b>
  ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
  <b>Cluster size:</b> 3 nodes
  <b>Majority:</b> ceil(3/2) = 2 nodes
  <b>Result:</b> Leader + 1 follower = 2 ✅
  → <b>Safe to commit</b>
end note

Leader -> LogLeader : Mark index 100 as <b>COMMITTED</b>
activate LogLeader #FFE0B2
LogLeader --> Leader : OK
deactivate LogLeader

Leader --> Client : ✅ <b>Success</b> Reservation ID: res_abc123
deactivate Leader

par <color:#6A1B9A><b>Notify Followers to Commit</b></color>

    Leader -> Follower1 : <b>Commit notification</b> commitIndex: 100
    activate Follower1 #E1BEE7
    Follower1 -> LogF1 : Mark as committed
    activate LogF1 #FFE0B2
    LogF1 --> Follower1 : OK
    deactivate LogF1
    deactivate Follower1

else <color:#6A1B9A><b>Parallel Path</b></color>

    Leader -> Follower2 : <b>Commit notification</b> commitIndex: 100
    activate Follower2 #E1BEE7
    Follower2 -> LogF2 : Mark as committed
    activate LogF2 #FFE0B2
    LogF2 --> Follower2 : OK
    deactivate LogF2
    deactivate Follower2

end

' ============================================
' Scenario 2: Concurrent Requests
' ============================================

== Scenario 2: Race Condition Prevention ==

participant "<color:white><b>Client A</b></color>" as ClientA CLIENT_COLOR
participant "<color:white><b>Client B</b></color>" as ClientB CLIENT_COLOR

note over ClientA, ClientB #FFEBEE
  <b><color:#B71C1C>Race Condition Scenario</color></b>
  ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
  Both clients try to reserve last item

  <b>Traditional DB:</b> Both might succeed → Overselling ❌
  <b>Raft:</b> Leader serializes → Only one succeeds ✅
end note

ClientA -> Leader : **Reserve 1 unit** SKU: IPHONE-15 contract: ctr_111
activate Leader #AED581
ClientB -> Leader : **Reserve 1 unit** SKU: IPHONE-15 contract: ctr_222

note right of Leader #FFEBEE
  <b><color:#B71C1C>Serialization</color></b>
  ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
  Leader processes sequentially:
  1. Request A → Check stock (1 available) ✅
  2. Request B → Check stock (0 available) ❌
end note

Leader -> LogLeader : Append Index 101 (Client A)
activate LogLeader #FFF59D
LogLeader --> Leader : Stock: 1 → 0
deactivate LogLeader

Leader --> ClientA : ✅ **Success** res_111
deactivate Leader

activate LogLeader #AED581
Leader -> LogLeader : Try append Index 102 (Client B)
activate LogLeader #FFF59D
LogLeader --> Leader : ❌ **Insufficient stock** (0 available)
deactivate LogLeader

Leader --> ClientB : ❌ **Out of stock**
deactivate Leader

note right of Leader #FFEBEE
  <b><color:#B71C1C>Race Condition Prevented</color></b>
  ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
  Leader's sequential processing
  ensures linearizability.

  <b>Guarantee:</b> No two clients can
  reserve the same stock unit ✅
end note

' ============================================
' Scenario 3: Leader Failure
' ============================================

== Scenario 3: Leader Failure & Election ==

Client -> Leader : Reserve request
activate Leader #AED581

Leader --> Leader : ❌ **CRASH** (network failure)
note right of Leader #FFEBEE
  <b><color:#C62828>Leader Failed</color></b>
  ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
  - Network partition
  - Hardware failure
  - Software crash
end note

... Wait for heartbeat timeout (150-300ms) ...

note over Follower1, Follower2 #FFF9C4
  <b><color:#F57C00>Election Timeout</color></b>
  ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
  No heartbeat from leader
  → Followers start election
end note

Follower1 -> Follower1 : Start election Increment term: 6
activate Follower1 #CE93D8

Follower1 -> Follower2 : **RequestVote RPC** Term: 6, Candidate: Node 2
activate Follower2 #CE93D8
Follower2 --> Follower1 : ✅ **Vote granted**
deactivate Follower2

Follower1 -> Follower1 : **Majority votes** (2 out of 2 available) → Become LEADER

note right of Follower1 #C8E6C9
  <b><color:#2E7D32>New Leader Elected</color></b>
  ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
  Node 2 is now leader (Term 6)
  Election time: 150-300ms
  → System operational again
end note

Follower1 -> Follower1 : Replay uncommitted log entries
deactivate Follower1

Client -> Follower1 : **Retry reserve request**
activate Follower1 #C5E1A5
note right of Follower1 #E3F2FD
  <b><color:#1976D2>Automatic Retry</color></b>
  ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
  Client automatically
  retries to new leader
end note

Follower1 -> LogF1 : Append index 103
activate LogF1 #FFF59D
LogF1 --> Follower1 : OK
deactivate LogF1

Follower1 -> Follower2 : Replicate
activate Follower2 #CE93D8
Follower2 --> Follower1 : ACK
deactivate Follower2

Follower1 --> Client : ✅ **Success**
deactivate Follower1

' ============================================
' Log Structure Example
' ============================================

note over LogLeader, LogF2 #FFF9C4
  <b><color:#F57C00>Raft Log Structure</color></b>
  ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  Index | Term | Operation                           | Status
  ─────┼──────┼─────────────────────────────────────┼──────────
  98   | 5    | RESERVE MACBOOK-PRO, qty=1          | COMMITTED
  99   | 5    | RESERVE AIRPODS-PRO, qty=2          | COMMITTED
  100  | 5    | RESERVE IPHONE-15, qty=1            | COMMITTED
  101  | 5    | RESERVE IPHONE-15, qty=1 (Client A) | COMMITTED
  102  | 5    | REJECT (insufficient stock)         | COMMITTED
  103  | 6    | RESERVE MACBOOK-AIR, qty=1          | COMMITTED

  <b><color:#F57C00>Properties:</color></b>
  - Append-only (immutable)
  - Sequentially numbered
  - Replicated across cluster
  - Majority consensus required
  - Leader elected on failure
end note

' ============================================
' Summary
' ============================================

note over Client, LogF2 #E8F5E9
  <size:14><b><color:#1B5E20>Raft Consensus Benefits</color></b></size>
  ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  ✅ <b>Linearizability</b>
     All operations appear in single, total order
     → No race conditions

  ✅ <b>Fault Tolerance</b>
     Survives (N-1)/2 node failures
     3 nodes → 1 failure tolerated
     5 nodes → 2 failures tolerated

  ✅ <b>Consistency</b>
     Majority quorum ensures data durability
     Committed data never lost

  ✅ <b>No Overselling</b>
     Leader serializes all stock operations
     Concurrent requests processed sequentially

  <b><color:#1B5E20>Performance</color></b>
  • Latency: 50-200ms per operation
  • Throughput: 10,000 req/s per cluster
  • Election time: 150-300ms
end note

legend right
  <size:14><b>Raft Consensus Color Legend</b></size>
  ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
  |<back:#B71C1C><color:white>     </color></back>| <b>Raft Leader</b> | Serializes all requests |
  |<back:#6A1B9A><color:white>     </color></back>| <b>Raft Follower</b> | Replicates log, votes |
  |<back:#1976D2><color:white>     </color></back>| <b>Client</b> | Inventory service |
  |<back:#F57C00><color:white>     </color></back>| <b>Replicated Log</b> | Distributed state |

  <size:11><b>Key Properties:</b></size>
  • <b>Linearizability:</b> Total order of operations
  • <b>Fault Tolerance:</b> Survives (N-1)/2 failures
  • <b>Consistency:</b> Majority quorum guarantees
  • <b>No Overselling:</b> Race conditions prevented
endlegend

@enduml
